c.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7799025/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review repeatedly describes \\"local\\" initiators, tissue microenvironments and region-specific (gateway) neural activation as causes of IL‑6 (and other proinflammatory mediators, including TNFα) production via the IL‑6 amplifier. It thus presents mechanistic and experimental evidence that spatially localized events and tissue-scale phenomena can drive IL‑6/TNFα–mediated inflammation. Therefore the claim of no causal relationship between spatial scale (locality) and proinflammatory processes is contradicted by the citations."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/immunology/articles/10.3389/fimmu.2024.1330386/full", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review/meta-analysis examines associations of IL-6, TNF-α and IL‑1β with age-related disease and does not discuss \\"spatial scale\\" or any mechanisms linking spatial scale to cytokine levels (or vice versa). Because the source contains no information about spatial scale, it cannot substantiate a claim about the absence of a causal relationship between spatial scale and proinflammatory cytokines."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-85514-0", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reports correlations between peripheral IL-6/TNF-α and resting-state functional connectivity measured using a particular brain parcellation, and explicitly states its cross-sectional design prevents causal inference. It does not evaluate or provide evidence about \\"spatial scale\\" causing changes in cytokine levels (or cytokines causing changes in spatial scale). Therefore the citation does not support the strong claim that no causal relationship exists between spatial scale and proinflammatory processes — it simply does not address that causal question.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Spatial Scale does not cause Proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which adjusting or considering spatial scale would alter levels of TNF-alpha or IL-6. Likewise, changes in proinflammatory processes do not cause spatial scale to change. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.255836948394831, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8676485242627937, 'min_prob': 0.04731838584861546, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0014568977902430708, 'prob_variance': 0.0576131883071101, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.958434896109027, 'avg_nll': 0.22780224146191905}

