   Properties: {'session_id': '1c04e2f2-6dfb-4cfe-a8f3-cfb5de2b8be4', 'prob_std': 0.2473528844526858, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10915202/', 'https://www.annualreviews.org/content/journals/10.1146/annurev.so.18.080192.000311', 'https://www.psypost.org/your-social-status-has-a-surprising-influence-on-your-biological-stress-responses/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7833036484161363, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10915202/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited study models perceived stress as a mediator of effects from perceived social support to mental-health outcomes and finds social support predicts lower perceived stress. It is cross-sectional and explicitly notes it cannot establish causality. The paper provides correlations (stress associated with lower family/partner support) but does not test or provide evidence that perceived stress causally changes perceived social support, nor does it demonstrate a mechanism for such a causal path. However, the study does not prove the absence of any causal effect from stress → perceived support. Therefore the citation is consistent with treating stress as an outcome of support (not the reverse) and with caution about causal claims, but it does not definitively support the stronger claim that PSS cannot causally affect MSPSS. \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Perceived stress (PSS) does not causally cause perceived social support (MSPSS) to change. There is no direct mechanism by which experiencing more or less stress would directly alter one's perception of social support. If any association exists, it is likely explained by mediating variables or reverse causality, but not a direct causal link from PSS to MSPSS.", 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3043788112307069, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8382559373291435, 'min_prob': 0.03165152855977425, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002727857556763313, 'prob_variance': 0.06118344944706373, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1450335711194577, 'avg_nll': 0.26572692072772885}

