nts. The paper frames effects via stress appraisal (perceived stress), not reduced exposure, and does not test independence from coping styles or cognitive style. Therefore the specific mechanism and the outcome (lower rumination, independent of coping/cognitive style) asserted in the explanation are not supported by the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Perceived social support (MSPSS) leads to a decrease in rumination (CERQ-R) because individuals who receive high levels of social support are less exposed to challenging or stressful life events. As a result, they encounter fewer situations that could trigger repetitive negative thinking. In this way, the protective environment fostered by perceived social support (MSPSS) minimizes the likelihood of experiencing adversity, which directly translates to lower levels of rumination (CERQ-R), independent of individual coping skills or cognitive style.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Perceived social support (MSPSS) leads to a decrease in rumination (CERQ-R) because individuals who receive high levels of social support are less exposed to challenging or stressful life events. As a result, they encounter fewer situations that could trigger repetitive negative thinking. In this way, the protective environment fostered by perceived social support (MSPSS) minimizes the likelihood of experiencing adversity, which directly translates to lower levels of rumination (CERQ-R), independent of individual coping skills or cognitive style.', 'perplexity': 1.4542206768866288, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8046300047513896, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.01672530042888471, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004312204514546691, 'prob_variance': 0.07849682349753304, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0175333892226828, 'avg_nll': 0.3744701398692413}

