ficient to support the asserted \\"NONE\\" causal relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where Loneliness (UCLS) causes Daily hassles (HS) or vice versa. While these variables may be correlated in some contexts, there is no clear mechanism by which one directly and causally influences the other without mediation. Any observed connection is likely explained by other variables such as perceived stress or social support.', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3841413870180515, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8194010100395265, 'min_prob': 0.03701944019157038, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003952302896135858, 'prob_variance': 0.0747978678762726, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.893046056832963, 'avg_nll': 0.3250800102277163}

