e evidence that higher BMI causes lower mindfulness or that increased weight reduces present-moment attention due to discomfort/self-consciousness."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1740144511001793", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The provided citation contains only an error message and no substantive content or evidence relating BMI to mindfulness. There is nothing in the cited material that supports the claimed negative relationship or the proposed mechanism (physical discomfort and self-consciousness reducing present-moment awareness)."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher body mass index (BMI) leads to lower mindfulness because increased body weight is thought to cause greater physical discomfort and self-consciousness, which distracts individuals from being present in the moment. As a result, people with higher BMI scores are less able to practice mindfulness effectively.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher body mass index (BMI) leads to lower mindfulness because increased body weight is thought to cause greater physical discomfort and self-consciousness, which distracts individuals from being present in the moment. As a result, people with higher BMI scores are less able to practice mindfulness effectively.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

