ect causal relationship exists between IL-6/TNF-α and prosocial behavior."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) cause prosocial behavior (PGG) or vice versa. While there may be correlations or complex indirect pathways involving psychological or physiological mediators, no clear direct mechanism links these variables causally. Therefore, they should not be connected directly in a causal loop diagram.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.421432100052545, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8049400140882508, 'min_prob': 0.033144761347823216, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00341228902659502, 'prob_variance': 0.07910382393471899, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1971579797064784, 'avg_nll': 0.3516648845611334}

