ion content."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/neuroscience/interleukin-10", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains only an error message and no usable content or evidence. It provides no information linking IL-10 or anti-inflammatory processes to reductions in frequency or perception of daily hassles or to calming stress-related neural circuits, so the claim is unsupported by the provided citation.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher levels of anti-inflammatory processes, such as increased IL-10, directly reduce the frequency or perceived intensity of daily hassles. This occurs because IL-10 not only modulates immune responses but also calms neural circuits associated with stress perception, making individuals less likely to notice or report daily hassles.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher levels of anti-inflammatory processes, such as increased IL-10, directly reduce the frequency or perceived intensity of daily hassles. This occurs because IL-10 not only modulates immune responses but also calms neural circuits associated with stress perception, making individuals less likely to notice or report daily hassles.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

