out causal links or mediation pathways from rumination to BMI (via depression, activity, or sleep). Therefore the citation does not substantiate the claim that rumination has no direct causal effect on BMI or that any effect would be mediated by the named variables."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) does not directly cause Body mass index (BMI) to change. Any effect of rumination on BMI would likely be mediated by other variables such as depressive symptoms, physical inactivity, or sleep disturbance, which are already present in the CLD. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship from rumination to BMI.', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.1576501938847816, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9005450239097322, 'min_prob': 0.1405101350162383, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0017389689774162643, 'prob_variance': 0.038127230721017764, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.6266332473139324, 'avg_nll': 0.14639225569640363}

