ts the claimed negative relationship overall and does not substantiate the proposed mechanism."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'It is possible that as depressive symptoms increase, individuals may actually experience fewer sleep disturbances because they become more fatigued and thus sleep more soundly. Additionally, depressive symptoms can sometimes lead to increased need for rest, resulting in improved sleep quality and fewer reported issues on the PSQI.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'It is possible that as depressive symptoms increase, individuals may actually experience fewer sleep disturbances because they become more fatigued and thus sleep more soundly. Additionally, depressive symptoms can sometimes lead to increased need for rest, resulting in improved sleep quality and fewer reported issues on the PSQI.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

