ed source is available, the explanation is not supported by the citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Physical inactivity (SBQ) leads to increased depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) because extended periods of sedentary behavior directly cause neurochemical imbalances in the brain that result in mood disturbances. Therefore, higher scores on physical inactivity (SBQ) inherently trigger more severe depressive symptoms (IDS-SR), regardless of other lifestyle or psychosocial factors. Conversely, reducing physical inactivity (SBQ) will automatically resolve depressive symptoms (IDS-SR), as physical movement itself is sufficient to restore psychological well-being.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Physical inactivity (SBQ) leads to increased depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) because extended periods of sedentary behavior directly cause neurochemical imbalances in the brain that result in mood disturbances. Therefore, higher scores on physical inactivity (SBQ) inherently trigger more severe depressive symptoms (IDS-SR), regardless of other lifestyle or psychosocial factors. Conversely, reducing physical inactivity (SBQ) will automatically resolve depressive symptoms (IDS-SR), as physical movement itself is sufficient to restore psychological well-being.', 'perplexity': 1.360482224348911, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8203109335703823, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.016018411271533278, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00457477822821869, 'prob_variance': 0.07050931834635593, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9688161888807574, 'avg_nll': 0.30783921362762906}

