0", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains only an error message and provides no substantive content or evidence. Therefore it cannot support the claim that proinflammatory processes do not directly cause BMI changes.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) do not directly cause body mass index (BMI) to change. While BMI can influence proinflammatory markers, there is no established causal pathway where changes in proinflammatory processes directly alter BMI. Any association is likely mediated by other variables such as metabolic rate, physical activity, or adiposity, which are not direct effects.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3573420807511685, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8093656743591366, 'min_prob': 0.04938850534741535, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0041033547837887, 'prob_variance': 0.06933071904782757, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.099049627984482, 'avg_nll': 0.3055284351206193}

