erdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) cause prosocial behavior (PGG) or vice versa. Current scientific understanding does not support a direct mechanism linking changes in IL-10 levels to changes in prosocial behavior. Any associations are likely mediated by other variables such as psychological states or inflammatory processes. Therefore, no direct causal link should be included in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3287687886522528, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8369544846396465, 'min_prob': 0.023036839228941373, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0018709955865890647, 'prob_variance': 0.06533095099773484, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.018625850854072, 'avg_nll': 0.2842527906698193}

