44. Rumination (CERQ-R)-[NEGATIVE]->Proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) causes proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) to increase through sustained psychological stress, which activates physiological stress pathways and elevates inflammatory biomarkers. Increased rumination prolongs stress responses, leading to higher levels of TNF-alpha and IL-6. Conversely, reducing rumination would decrease these proinflammatory processes. This causal link is supported by psychoneuroimmunology research on stress and inflammation.', 'session_id': '2bb1b40f-22fb-4ef4-855a-2ec03706796a', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8957598/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4849278/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0149763422000094', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32087393/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumination_(psychology)'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8957598/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited scoping review and included studies do not support a general negative relationship. Most experimental manipulations of rumination produced increases (or greater reactivity) in inflammatory markers (e.g., CRP, salivary IL‑1β, stress‑related IL‑6), and longitudinal/interaction analyses more often link higher rumination to higher inflammation or show no association. Only isolated, sample‑specific or subtype findings (e.g., a negative association with IL‑4 in one pregnant sample, a gender‑specific negative coupling for stimulated cytokines in women, or protective effects for reflective [non‑negative] thinking) reported reductions; these are inconsistent and limited. Overall the evidence points toward positive or null associations, not a consistent negative relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4849278/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reaso