e depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) cause perceived stress (PSS). While these variables are often correlated, causality typically runs from perceived stress to depressive symptoms, not the reverse. No direct mechanism exists whereby increases in depressive symptoms causally increase perceived stress.', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3761610855802184, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8188249563724935, 'min_prob': 0.0637860433351568, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004757864334555977, 'prob_variance': 0.07118424678028261, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1220188690427597, 'avg_nll': 0.319297800668107}

